C:\Users\Jason\Documents\Jason\Orchestrator_Harness\Firmware\fresh-experiments\S11_20260821-plan2-suite-012\.agent-workspace\suite012_s11_boreal_replacement_002_codex.jsonl:18:{"type":"user","uuid":"e1e4ddff-0908-4f17-bdad-3ad5a3f2d754","session_id":"cb916473-1240-43a0-9a58-d24373d5f240","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_9om1up06","is_error":false,"content":"# Test Specification — S11: Fresh nRF setup from datasheet\n\n- Identity: `S11`, doer `Boreal`, server commit `61e7efc747f66d39263020265aa608950b0d281b`, authored 2026-08-21 by `PLAN2.SUITE.MANAGER.014`.\n- Objective: independently derive fresh setup for both nRF DKs from empty repositories using friendly name, truthfully established `nRF52840-QIAA`, supplied PDF, UART requirement, and correlated electronic identity; keep J-Link/VCOM identities distinct.\n- Excluded: PCA/PCB/photo/visual prerequisites, flash, radio, physical manipulation, prior semantic credit, direct probe tools, hidden profiles, or operator input.\n- Hardware: NRF-A nRF52840 DK probe `683710208` VCOM `COM16`; NRF-B probe `683854191` VCOM `COM15`. Correlated official BOM/electronic evidence establishes QIAA. CoreSX1262 wiring is not exercised.\n- Authority: suite-012 ordinary non-destructive setup/validation/connect/disconnect; exact current assignment, identity, plan and permission remain mandatory. Final state is both logically disconnected and unchanged.\n- Dependencies: none. Boreal owns NRF-A/NRF-B internal shards. HIL exclusively leases both boards, probes/VCOMs, Nordic enumeration scope, Boreal provider/workspace/cache, and isolated S11 MCP/state/artifact roots. Board-free preparation starts immediately; no build handoff.\n- Safe boundary after complete MCP calls/disconnect; calls 60 seconds, two guided correction attempts, 90-second pause bound.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### REQ-001 — independent setup\n\nFor each shard execute handshake → overview → setup-tool load → populated setup plan → setup with allowed inputs only. PASS requires distinct project-local PDF/evidence, exact probe/VCOM bindings and no hidden profile or marketing-name package inference. Preserve ordered raw calls, manifests and hashes.\n\n### REQ-002 — identical-board repair\n\nIntentionally select the other Nordic board once, retain its specific mismatch/refusal, then use server-directed continuation. PASS requires no silent retarget and no readiness grant to the other shard. Preserve refusal/remedy/continuation and both identities.\n\n### REQ-003 — validation and lifecycle\n\nRun safety refresh, validate, status, connect, board-info and disconnect for both. PASS requires separate code/UART readiness, distinct J-Link/VCOM routing, no leakage, and clean disconnect. Preserve raw responses and final status.\n\nSeed is only the wrong-board choice. Require schema-valid result/report and raw evidence. PASS requires both genuinely fresh shards.\n"}]}}
